# ...but Google's attestation roots are PUBLIC trust anchors, not credentials,
# and `*.pem` above was silently swallowing them. The consequence was not a
# quiet one: `loadRoots()` fails fast by design, so the file never reaching the
# image took the whole service down on deploy (Render, 2026-08-06 — "ENOENT:
# /app/backend/data/google-attestation-roots.pem", exit status 1).
#
# The rule above is kept exactly as it is: a blanket `*.pem` ban is the right
# default when the same tree holds signing material, and weakening it to fix one
# public file would trade a deploy failure for a leaked-key risk. This is a
# single-file exception instead, and it is only correct while the file stays what
# it claims to be — PUBLIC certificates. Verified before un-ignoring: the file
# contains 2 CERTIFICATE blocks and no PRIVATE KEY block. Re-check that before
# adding any further exception here.
!backend/data/google-attestation-roots.pem

